<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Quadrotor: Powerloop Maneuver</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The quadrotor state is <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=[\mathbf{p}^{\top},\mathbf{v}^{\top},\mathbf{q}^{\top}]^{\top}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=[\mathbf{p}^{\top},\mathbf{v}^{\top},\mathbf{q}^{\top}]^{\top}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{10}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the input is thrust <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{a_{\text{cmd}}}\in[0,4g]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{a_{\text{cmd}}}\in[0,4g]</annotation></semantics></math> and body rates <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}}=[\omega_{x},\omega_{y},\omega_{z}]^{\top}\in[-18,18]^{3}\,\mathrm{rad/s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>rad</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}}=[\omega_{x},\omega_{y},\omega_{z}]^{\top}\in[-18,18]^{3}\,\mathrm{rad/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The reference is a powerloop inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>: starting at <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.5</annotation></semantics></math> m/s, the quadrotor tracks a vertical loop of radius <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math> m centered at <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,0,2]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,0,2]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> m while executing a <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> flip. The safe set is <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:p_{z}\leq 3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:p_{z}\leq 3\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Although the safety specification is a single altitude bound, the constraint is enforced through the full <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional dynamics and all actuations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14536v1/figures/quadrotor-iris-ps2.png" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/160;" width="381" height="160" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Safe-arrival policies in action: (left) <math id="S5.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;" mathcolor="#003B67">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;" mathcolor="#003B67">SA</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;" mathcolor="#003B67">θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.F3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;"> learned policy</span> and (middle) <math id="S5.F3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#8C3B00;" mathcolor="#8C3B00">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#8C3B00;" mathcolor="#8C3B00">SA</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.F3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#8C3B00;"> analytic policy</span>. The <span id="S5.F3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#D8A33A;">base set trajectory segments</span> are controlled by the <span id="S5.F3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#D8A33A;">base controller <math id="S5.F3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D8A33A;" mathcolor="#D8A33A">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#D8A33A;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#D8A33A">ℬ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>. (Right) PS2 policies tracking the powerloop reference (dashed line): <span id="S5.F3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;">PS2<sub id="S5.F3.12.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.F3.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SA</span></sub></span> with <math id="S5.F3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;" mathcolor="#003B67">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;" mathcolor="#003B67">SA</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#003B67;" mathcolor="#003B67">θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S5.F3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#8C3B00;">PS2<sub id="S5.F3.13.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.F3.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ABP</span></sub></span> with <math id="S5.F3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#8C3B00;" mathcolor="#8C3B00">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#8C3B00;" mathcolor="#8C3B00">SA</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Quadrotor: Powerloop Maneuver ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that PS2<sub id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SA</span></sub> is the best-performing method among all policies with <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\%</annotation></semantics></math> safety.
Relative to PS2<sub id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ABP</span></sub>, it reduces all RMSEs by approximately <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="57\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>57</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">57\%</annotation></semantics></math>.
Compared to MPS, it reduces <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math>-RMSE by about <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70\%</annotation></semantics></math> despite MPS being given a longer recovery horizon. The penalty and CBF-RL baselines still exhibit violations, and the CMDP baselines show the limitation of enforcing safety only in expectation. The learned <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is especially important in this agile setting.
Fig. <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.2 Quadrotor: Powerloop Maneuver ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> recovers from task-relevant near-ceiling states much better compared to the analytic policy.
Quantitatively, the learned safe-arrival policy increases task-relevant recoverability from <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.9\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="85.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>85.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">85.9\%</annotation></semantics></math> over the analytic backup, with the largest gains near the ceiling (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="35.5\%\!\to\!69.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>35.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>69.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">35.5\%\!\to\!69.3\%</annotation></semantics></math>).
This larger near-ceiling safe-arrival set explains the downstream tracking performance gap in Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Quadrotor: Powerloop Maneuver ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
