</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we review prior work related to our proposed framework. We organize existing methods into five categories.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Safe RL via Constrained Policy Optimization.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This line of work imposes constraints from learned value functions through constrained policy optimization, such as Lagrangian methods.
A widely adopted formulation is the constrained Markov decision process (CMDP) framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, where an auxiliary cost function is introduced and the expected trajectory cost is constrained to remain below a predefined threshold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.
More recently, state-wise safe RL methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> have gained attention: instead of enforcing safety in expectation through a cost value function, they learn a neural certificate function and impose it as a constraint to encourage state-wise safety <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. However, neither class of methods can guarantee the safety of the learned policy.
First, the constraints are provided by learned neural-network values, which are not provably reliable in general.
Second, constrained policy optimization itself does not guarantee that the outputs of the policy network will satisfy the imposed constraints.
Although these methods scale to expressive policies and high-dimensional systems, and can achieve good empirical performance in some cases, catastrophic failures may still occur during deployment due to the lack of formal safety guarantees.
This gap motivates the study of provably safe RL.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Safe RL via Verified Certificate.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A second line of work attaches a formal safety certificate to the policy.
Unlike neural certificate functions learned purely from loss functions, formal safety guarantees require the synthesis and verification of a valid certificate.
Common certificate functions include control barrier function (CBF) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, safety index (SI) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, and reachability value function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>.
Although they take different forms, these certificates can be viewed as functional representations of control-invariant sets, characterizing states from which persistent safety can be maintained under an admissible controller.
In safe RL, such certificates are typically used as safety filters or shields that modify unsafe actions proposed by a learned policy  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The main challenge is that obtaining a valid certificate amounts to synthesizing or verifying a control-invariant set, which poses significant scalability challenges.
Hamilton–Jacobi (HJ) reachability analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> provides a formal mathematical framework for computing maximal control-invariant sets for nonlinear systems.
However, it requires solving a nonlinear partial differential equation (PDE) over a discretized state space, whose computational cost scales exponentially with the state dimension.
Sum-of-squares (SOS) optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> synthesizes polynomial safety certificates by relaxing polynomial nonnegativity conditions into SOS constraints, which can be solved via semidefinite programming.
While effective for polynomial dynamics and semialgebraic safe sets, SOS methods scale poorly with state dimension and polynomial degree, and often produce conservative invariant sets that are much smaller than the maximal sets computed by HJ reachability when the latter is tractable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Compared to the above approaches, PS2-RL avoids the fundamental bottleneck of explicit invariant-set synthesis by learning a backup policy that induces an implicit control-invariant set online.
This implicit set is then used to provide formal safety guarantees while enabling scalability to higher-dimensional systems.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Backup Control Barrier Functions.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our framework builds on the backup control barrier function (BCBF) framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>.
During online deployment, a BCBF certifies the set of states from which a fixed deterministic backup policy can return the system to a small base set within a finite horizon while remaining inside the safe set.
This construction yields an implicit control-invariant set, whose associated safety-filter constraint is of relative degree one by construction and can explicitly account for input limits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>.
However, the backup policy is typically hand-designed, such as an LQR around an equilibrium <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, and the resulting implicit invariant set is therefore often limited in size <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>.
PS2-RL departs from this line of work in two key aspects.
First, we learn the backup policy using the proposed safe-arrival value function, which characterizes time-optimal safe recovery to the base set.
Second, the BCBF constraints are embedded into a control-invariant layer via differentiable projection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, enabling the RL policy to be trained end-to-end while preserving formal safety guarantees, rather than using the safety filter only as a post-hoc correction during deployment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RL for Reach-Avoid Specifications.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optimal control for reach-avoid specifications <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> jointly captures the objective of reaching a target set while avoiding a failure set, making it a natural formulation for designing backup policies.
However, classical optimal-control approaches for reach-avoid tasks are computationally expensive and quickly become intractable for high-dimensional systems.
More recently, RL-based methods have been proposed to solve reach-avoid problems with improved scalability, making them more tractable for complex dynamical systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hsu et al. [23]</a></cite> propose a time-discounted reach-avoid Bellman equation built from dense target and safety-margin functions, typically instantiated with signed-distance-like geometric quantities inside a nested max–min backup.
Although this formulation captures reach-avoid semantics, the learned critic depends not only on the logical event of reaching the target before failure, but also on the choice, scale, and geometry of these task-specific shaping functions.
This makes the optimization sensitive and difficult in practice: stable learning requires warm-starting with a standard RL objective and progressively annealing the discount factor.
In contrast, our method learns an indicator-style probabilistic critic that directly represents the safe-arrival event.
The critic is aligned with the underlying reach-avoid specification rather than an auxiliary dense geometric surrogate, leading to cleaner credit assignment and easier optimization.
As a result, our RL implementation follows a standard training pipeline and learns effective policies without task-specific heuristics.
Moreover, although our main theoretical development focuses on deterministic systems and deterministic backup policies, the safe-arrival value function is probabilistic by construction and naturally extends to stochastic dynamics and stochastic policies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Differentiable Optimization Layers.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This line of work embeds optimization problems as differentiable layers inside neural networks.
OptNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> differentiates through quadratic programs via implicit differentiation of the Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) conditions, enabling constrained optimization modules to be trained end-to-end.
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HardNet</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> provides a unified framework for efficiently training neural networks under general affine and convex constraints, with universal-approximation guarantees for networks equipped with such constrained layers. Recent variants include LMI-Net <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>, which specializes to linear matrix inequalities, and HardNet++ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, which handles more general nonlinear constraints.
The control-invariant layer proposed in PS2-RL inherits the universal-approximation guarantee of <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HardNet-CVX</span>.
Unlike prior differentiable layers, however, its constraints are not specified directly in closed form; instead, they are induced by the rollout of a learned backup policy.
This allows PS2-RL to enforce rollout-based control invariance while retaining the expressiveness needed for high-performance policies on high-dimensional systems.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Background on Safe Control Theory</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides the safe control background used in Sec. <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Backup Control Barrier Functions ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1.SSS1" title="4.1.1 BCBF-constrained policies under a fixed backup policy ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1.1</span></a>.
We focus on the deterministic, control-affine system (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Backup Control Barrier Functions ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) in Sec. <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Backup Control Barrier Functions ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
For convenience, the system is restated below:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{x}=f(x)+g(x)u,\qquad x\in{\mathcal{X}}\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}^{n},\quad u\in{\mathcal{U}}\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}^{m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{x}=f(x)+g(x)u,\qquad x\in{\mathcal{X}}\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}^{n},\quad u\in{\mathcal{U}}\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}^{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes actuator limits and <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state space of interest.
The functions <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> are assumed locally Lipschitz, so that the closed-loop trajectories are well defined under the feedback policies considered in this work.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Control Invariance</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in Sec. <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Backup Control Barrier Functions ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, safety of the system (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In Appendix C Background on Safe Control Theory ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) is specified through a safe set</p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{S}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{\mathcal{S}}(x)\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{S}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{\mathcal{S}}(x)\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\mathcal{S}}:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\mathcal{S}}:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable.
Importantly, not every state in <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is necessarily safe in the dynamical sense.
Under bounded inputs, there may be states inside <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> from which all admissible control inputs eventually lead to a safety violation.
Thus, safe control typically seeks an invariant subset of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, rather than enforcing membership in <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> alone <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Control Invariance)<span id="A3.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A set <math id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is control-invariant if there exists a state-feedback policy <math id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for every initial condition <math id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(0)\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(0)\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding closed-loop trajectory satisfies <math id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> forall <math id="A3.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This definition is the controlled analogue of Nagumo’s set-invariance condition <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>.
In the ideal case, one would compute the maximal control-invariant subset of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and restrict the controller to remain inside it.
However, computing such a set is difficult for nonlinear systems with input limits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Control Barrier Function</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Control barrier functions provide a differential certificate for such invariant subsets.
Let</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{C}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)\geq 0\}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{C}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)\geq 0\}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">be a candidate control-invariant set.
A control barrier function certifies that, at each point in <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an admissible input that prevents <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> from decreasing too quickly <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Control Barrier Function)<span id="A3.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A continuously differentiable function <math id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{C}}:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{C}}:{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a control barrier function (CBF) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> for the zero-superlevel set <math id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}:=\{x:h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)\geq 0\}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}:=\{x:h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)\geq 0\}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists an extended class-<math id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> function <math id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:{\mathbb{R}}\to{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:{\mathbb{R}}\to{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for all <math id="A3.Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left\{\nabla h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)^{\top}\left(f(x)+g(x)u\right)+\alpha(h_{\mathcal{C}}(x))\right\}\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left\{\nabla h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)^{\top}\left(f(x)+g(x)u\right)+\alpha(h_{\mathcal{C}}(x))\right\}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The condition (<a href="#A3.E20" title="In Definition C.2 (Control Barrier Function). ‣ C.2 Control Barrier Function ‣ Appendix C Background on Safe Control Theory ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) guarantees that the following state-dependent feasible input is nonempty:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathcal{C}}(x):=\left\{u\in{\mathcal{U}}:\nabla h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)^{\top}\left(f(x)+g(x)u\right)+\alpha(h_{\mathcal{C}}(x))\geq 0\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathcal{C}}(x):=\left\{u\in{\mathcal{U}}:\nabla h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)^{\top}\left(f(x)+g(x)u\right)+\alpha(h_{\mathcal{C}}(x))\geq 0\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">A standard CBF safety filter minimally modifies a nominal input <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by solving</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{u_{\mathrm{safe}}}(x)=\argmin_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left\|u-{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{u_{\mathrm{safe}}}(x)=\argmin_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left\|u-{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{s.t.}\quad\nabla h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)^{\top}\left(f(x)+g(x)u\right)+\kappa\left(h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)\right)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{s.t.}\quad\nabla h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)^{\top}\left(f(x)+g(x)u\right)+\kappa\left(h_{\mathcal{C}}(x)\right)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, this is a convex quadratic program since the CBF constraint (<a href="#A3.E20" title="In Definition C.2 (Control Barrier Function). ‣ C.2 Control Barrier Function ‣ Appendix C Background on Safe Control Theory ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) is affine in <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(CBF Invariance Guarantee)<span id="A3.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a CBF for <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a locally Lipschitz feedback policy
<math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(x)\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathcal{C}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x)\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathcal{C}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is forward
invariant under <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, if <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(0)\in{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(0)\in{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)\in{\mathcal{C}}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)\in{\mathcal{C}}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proof in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Cor. 2]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The main challenge is not using a CBF once it is known, but synthesizing a valid <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose superlevel set is control-invariant under the bounded input set <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The backup-CBF construction addresses this by avoiding the explicit synthesis of a global invariant set.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Backup Control Barrier Function</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Backup control barrier functions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> start from a small certified base set and enlarge it implicitly using the rollout of a deterministic backup policy. Let</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{B}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{\mathcal{B}}(x)\geq 0\}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{B}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{\mathcal{B}}(x)\geq 0\}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">be a known control-invariant base set, and let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{B}:{\mathcal{B}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{B}:{\mathcal{B}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a certified base controller.
In PS2-RL, this base pair is constructed locally around an equilibrium in Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Existence of a Certified Local Base Set). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
Let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}}:{\mathcal{X}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}}:{\mathcal{X}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a deterministic backup policy that agrees with the certified base controller on <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}}(x)=\pi_{B}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}}(x)=\pi_{B}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the closed-loop backup trajectory as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\pi_{b}}(x):=f(x)+g(x){\pi_{b}}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\pi_{b}}(x):=f(x)+g(x){\pi_{b}}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the corresponding flow map.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Backup-induced Control-Invariant Set)<span id="A3.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a backup horizon <math id="A3.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A3.Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-time backup-induced set is</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}}):=\mathcal{R}({\mathcal{B}},{\mathcal{S}},f_{\pi_{b}},T):=\left\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\in{\mathcal{B}}\;\wedge\;{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\in{\mathcal{S}}\quad\forall{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T]\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">∧</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}}):=\mathcal{R}({\mathcal{B}},{\mathcal{S}},f_{\pi_{b}},T):=\left\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\in{\mathcal{B}}\;\wedge\;{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\in{\mathcal{S}}\quad\forall{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> contains exactly the states from which the backup policy reaches the certified base set within time <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> while remaining in the safe set throughout the backup rollout.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Backup-Induced Invariance)<span id="A3.Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is control-invariant under <math id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}}=\pi_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}}=\pi_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}\subseteq{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}\subseteq{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> is control-invariant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proof in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, Thm. 1]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The set <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented as the zero-superlevel set of the implicit CBF</p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\mathcal{C}_{T}}(x)=\min\left\{\min_{{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T]}h_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right),\;h_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\right)\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\mathcal{C}_{T}}(x)=\min\left\{\min_{{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T]}h_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right),\;h_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\right)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The nonsmooth minimum in (<a href="#A3.E27" title="In C.3 Backup Control Barrier Function ‣ Appendix C Background on Safe Control Theory ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) makes a direct CBF-QP inconvenient. Instead, BCBF enforces sufficient CBF inequalities pointwise along the backup rollout and at the terminal base-set condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}}):=\frac{\partial{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})}{\partial x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}}):=\frac{\partial{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})}{\partial x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">denote the sensitivity of the backup flow with respect to its initial condition.
When <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\pi_{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\pi_{b}}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable, <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\pi_{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\pi_{b}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the variational equation</p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d{t^{\prime}}}\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})=\frac{\partial f_{\pi_{b}}}{\partial x}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}}),\qquad\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,0)=I." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d{t^{\prime}}}\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})=\frac{\partial f_{\pi_{b}}}{\partial x}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}}),\qquad\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,0)=I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For a candidate current input <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, define the rollout and terminal derivative terms</p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{D}}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{S}}(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{D}}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{S}}(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\nabla h_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)^{\top}\left[\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\big(f(x)+g(x)u\big)-f_{\pi_{b}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\nabla h_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)^{\top}\left[\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\big(f(x)+g(x)u\big)-f_{\pi_{b}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{D}}_{T}^{\mathcal{B}}(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{D}}_{T}^{\mathcal{B}}(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\nabla h_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\right)^{\top}\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,T)\big(f(x)+g(x)u\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\nabla h_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\right)^{\top}\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,T)\big(f(x)+g(x)u\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The subtraction term in <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> appears because the safety constraints along the backup rollout are indexed by future time.
As real time advances, the same future point on the backup rollout moves closer by the backup dynamics <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\pi_{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\pi_{b}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The terminal condition uses a fixed terminal horizon <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, so it has no corresponding subtraction term.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Given extended class-<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> functions <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the BCBF-admissible input set is</p>
<table id="A3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}}):=\big\{u\in{\mathcal{U}}:\;&{\mathcal{D}}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{S}}(x,u)+\alpha_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left(h_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)\right)\geq 0\quad\forall{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T],\\
&{\mathcal{D}}_{T}^{\mathcal{B}}(x,u)+\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left(h_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\right)\right)\geq 0\big\}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>𝕂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}}):=\big\{u\in{\mathcal{U}}:\;&amp;{\mathcal{D}}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{S}}(x,u)+\alpha_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left(h_{\mathcal{S}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})\right)\right)\geq 0\quad\forall{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T],\\
&amp;{\mathcal{D}}_{T}^{\mathcal{B}}(x,u)+\alpha_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left(h_{\mathcal{B}}\!\left({\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,T)\right)\right)\geq 0\big\}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">For fixed <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and fixed <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the rollout <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and sensitivity <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> are constants with respect to the optimization variable <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, all constraints in (<a href="#A3.E32" title="In C.3 Backup Control Barrier Function ‣ Appendix C Background on Safe Control Theory ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) are affine in <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> is convex whenever <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The corresponding BCBF-QP is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{u_{\mathrm{safe}}}(x)=\argmin_{u}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{u_{\mathrm{safe}}}(x)=\argmin_{u}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|u-{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|u-{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{s.t.}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{s.t.}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(BCBF Feasibility and Safety)<span id="A3.Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> is nonempty.
In particular, <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}}(x)\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}}(x)\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, any locally Lipschitz policy <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(x)\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x)\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> renders <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}})</annotation></semantics></math> forward invariant, and therefore keeps the trajectory inside <math id="A3.Thmproposition3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proof in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, Thm. 2]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, BCBFs also address the relative-degree issue that arises when the original safety function <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on states that are not directly actuated.
The composed functions <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{S}}\circ{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(\cdot,{t^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{S}}\circ{\Phi_{\pi_{b}}}(\cdot,{t^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> depend on the current input through the flow sensitivity <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\pi_{b}}(x,{t^{\prime}})g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under mild controllability and nondegeneracy assumptions, these composed constraints have relative degree one for positive rollout times <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, Thm. 3]</cite>.
This is why PS2-RL can specify safety directly in physically meaningful coordinates, such as altitude or lane position, without constructing high-order CBFs for the full system.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Safe-Arrival Value Function</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The safe-arrival value function is a central ingredient of Phase I (Sec. <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Phase I: Training the Safe-Arrival Policy ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>).
This section provides a formal characterization of the proposed value function and its key properties.
Although we introduce it for training the backup policy in our PS2-RL framework, the construction may be of independent interest and is not limited to the deterministic setting: the same methodology extends naturally to stochastic dynamics and randomized policies.
For this reason, we present the definitions in terms of trajectory laws, so that the notation applies directly to stochastic settings while reducing to pathwise statements in the deterministic case considered here.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a deterministic control system</p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{k+1}=F(x_{k},u_{k}),\qquad x_{k}\in{\mathcal{X}},\quad u_{k}\in{\mathcal{U}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{k+1}=F(x_{k},u_{k}),\qquad x_{k}\in{\mathcal{X}},\quad u_{k}\in{\mathcal{U}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">together with deterministic policies <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:{\mathcal{X}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:{\mathcal{X}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the base set, let <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the safe set, and define the failure set by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{F}}:={\mathcal{X}}\setminus{\mathcal{S}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{F}}:={\mathcal{X}}\setminus{\mathcal{S}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The continuation set is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{H}}:={\mathcal{X}}\setminus({\mathcal{B}}\cup{\mathcal{F}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{H}}:={\mathcal{X}}\setminus({\mathcal{B}}\cup{\mathcal{F}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Throughout, we assume <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}\cap{\mathcal{F}}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}\cap{\mathcal{F}}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> form a disjoint partition of <math id="A4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the indicators</p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{b}(x)=\mathbf{1}_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x),\qquad\mathbf{f}(x)=\mathbf{1}_{{\mathcal{F}}}(x),\qquad\mathbf{c}(x)=1-\mathbf{b}(x)-\mathbf{f}(x)=\mathbf{1}_{{\mathcal{H}}}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{b}(x)=\mathbf{1}_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x),\qquad\mathbf{f}(x)=\mathbf{1}_{{\mathcal{F}}}(x),\qquad\mathbf{c}(x)=1-\mathbf{b}(x)-\mathbf{f}(x)=\mathbf{1}_{{\mathcal{H}}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For an initial state-action pair <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a policy <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{x,u}^{\pi}=(x_{0},u_{0},x_{1},u_{1},\ldots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{x,u}^{\pi}=(x_{0},u_{0},x_{1},u_{1},\ldots)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">denote the rollout generated by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{0}=x,\qquad u_{0}=u,\qquad x_{k+1}=F(x_{k},u_{k})\ \text{for }k\geq 0,\qquad u_{k}=\pi(x_{k})\ \text{for }k\geq 1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{0}=x,\qquad u_{0}=u,\qquad x_{k+1}=F(x_{k},u_{k})\ \text{for }k\geq 0,\qquad u_{k}=\pi(x_{k})\ \text{for }k\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Because the dynamics and policy are deterministic, the rollout <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{x,u}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{x,u}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is unique.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> for the induced law on trajectory space and <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> for expectation with respect to this law. In the deterministic setting,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}=\delta_{\omega_{x,u}^{\pi}},\qquad\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}[Z]=Z(\omega_{x,u}^{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}=\delta_{\omega_{x,u}^{\pi}},\qquad\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}[Z]=Z(\omega_{x,u}^{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for every trajectory functional <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus any event depending only on the controlled rollout has probability either <math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. We keep the law-and-expectation notation because it remains unchanged when randomness is introduced into the policy or the dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The hitting times of the base and failure sets are the trajectory functionals</p>
<table id="A4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\mathcal{B}}(\omega)=\inf\{k\geq 0:x_{k}\in{\mathcal{B}}\},\qquad\tau_{\mathcal{F}}(\omega)=\inf\{k\geq 0:x_{k}\in{\mathcal{F}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\mathcal{B}}(\omega)=\inf\{k\geq 0:x_{k}\in{\mathcal{B}}\},\qquad\tau_{\mathcal{F}}(\omega)=\inf\{k\geq 0:x_{k}\in{\mathcal{F}}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with the convention <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf\emptyset=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf\emptyset=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. When the rollout is clear, we simply write <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The safe-arrival event is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{SA}}:=\{\omega:\tau_{\mathcal{B}}(\omega)&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}(\omega),\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}(\omega)&lt;\infty\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{SA}}:=\{\omega:\tau_{\mathcal{B}}(\omega)&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}(\omega),\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}(\omega)&lt;\infty\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">This event occurs exactly when the trajectory arrives at the base set in finite time before entering the failure set.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first define the undiscounted safe-arrival value. This value is the feasibility identifier associated with the safe-arrival specification: it identifies whether a policy succeeds in arriving at the base set before failure.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u):=\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{SA}})=\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u):=\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{SA}})=\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The associated state-value function is</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x):=Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,\pi(x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x):=Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,\pi(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The event-based definition admits an equivalent pathwise representation in terms of the indicator functions in (<a href="#A4.E38" title="In Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Indicator Representation of Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the empty product is interpreted as <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the pathwise quantity</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We show that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose first that <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}(x_{i})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}(x_{i})=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,\ldots,\tau_{\mathcal{B}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0,\ldots,\tau_{\mathcal{B}}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x_{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x_{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the term in <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}\notin{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}\notin{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x_{k})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x_{k})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the product <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> contains the factor <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}(x_{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}(x_{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore all terms except the term with <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> vanish, and <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conversely, suppose that the event <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}</annotation></semantics></math> does not occur. If the trajectory enters <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> before entering <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x_{k})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x_{k})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq\tau_{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq\tau_{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> the product contains the factor <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}(x_{\tau_{\mathcal{F}}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}(x_{\tau_{\mathcal{F}}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence every term in <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is zero. If the trajectory never enters <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x_{k})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x_{k})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, so again <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus (<a href="#A4.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ D.1 Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) holds pathwise. Taking expectation with respect to <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> gives (<a href="#A4.E46" title="In Proposition D.1 (Indicator Representation of Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.1 Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The indicator representation yields the following one-step self-consistency structure.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Self-Consistency Condition of Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\,Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}\!\left(F(x,u),\pi(F(x,u))\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\,Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}\!\left(F(x,u),\pi(F(x,u))\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Starting from (<a href="#A4.E46" title="In Proposition D.1 (Indicator Representation of Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.1 Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\mathbf{b}(x_{0})+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\mathbf{b}(x_{0})+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Re-indexing with <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=k-1</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{+}=F(x,u)=x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{+}=F(x,u)=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. From step <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> onward, the shifted rollout is the rollout initialized at <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{+},\pi(x^{+}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{+},\pi(x^{+}))</annotation></semantics></math> under the same policy <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right]=Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x^{+},\pi(x^{+}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right]=Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x^{+},\pi(x^{+})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{+}=F(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{+}=F(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math> proves the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The optimal undiscounted values are</p>
<table id="A4.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u):=\sup_{\pi}Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u),\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x):=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>π</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u):=\sup_{\pi}Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u),\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x):=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Since the first action <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed in <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math> and only the continuation policy remains to be optimized after the successor state, the optimal values satisfy</p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}\!\left(F(x,u),u^{+}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}\!\left(F(x,u),u^{+}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left[\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(F(x,u))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left[\mathbf{b}(x)+\mathbf{c}(x)V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(F(x,u))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The undiscounted value defines the states from which safe arrival is feasible.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Safe-arrival region)<span id="A4.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The deterministic safe-arrival region is</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}:=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of states from which there exists a deterministic policy that arrives at <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> before entering <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Minimum safe arrival time)<span id="A4.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle d(x):=\inf\Bigl\{k\in\{0,1,2,\ldots\}:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>:</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d(x):=\inf\Bigl\{k\in\{0,1,2,\ldots\}:</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \exists(u_{0},\ldots,u_{k-1})\in{\mathcal{U}}^{k}\ \text{such that}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">such that</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \exists(u_{0},\ldots,u_{k-1})\in{\mathcal{U}}^{k}\ \text{such that}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ x_{0}=x,\quad x_{i+1}=F(x_{i},u_{i})\ \text{for }i=0,\ldots,k-1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ x_{0}=x,\quad x_{i+1}=F(x_{i},u_{i})\ \text{for }i=0,\ldots,k-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ x_{i}\in{\mathcal{H}}\ \text{for all }i&lt;k,\quad x_{k}\in{\mathcal{B}}\Bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ x_{i}\in{\mathcal{H}}\ \text{for all }i&lt;k,\quad x_{k}\in{\mathcal{B}}\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with the convention <math id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> if the set above is empty. For <math id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the safety condition over <math id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math> is vacuous, so <math id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> exactly when <math id="A4.Thmdefinition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The following finite-step construction gives an equivalent characterization of the safe-arrival region.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite-step characterization of the safe-arrival region)<span id="A4.Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:={\mathcal{B}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:={\mathcal{B}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathcal{R}_{n}\cup\left\{x\in{\mathcal{H}}:\exists u\in{\mathcal{U}}\ \text{such that}\ F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{n}\right\},\qquad n\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">such that</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathcal{R}_{n}\cup\left\{x\in{\mathcal{H}}:\exists u\in{\mathcal{U}}\ \text{such that}\ F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{n}\right\},\qquad n\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\bigcup_{n=0}^{\infty}\mathcal{R}_{n}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:d(x)&lt;\infty\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\bigcup_{n=0}^{\infty}\mathcal{R}_{n}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:d(x)&lt;\infty\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for every <math id="A4.Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d(x)=\min\{n\geq 0:x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d(x)=\min\{n\geq 0:x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove by induction that <math id="A4.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if safe arrival from <math id="A4.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> can be achieved in at most <math id="A4.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>, this holds because <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0}={\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0}={\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose the claim holds for some <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then either <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case the induction hypothesis applies, or <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> and there exists <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the latter case, applying <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> for one step and then using the induction hypothesis from <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math> gives safe arrival in at most <math id="A4.SS1.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conversely, suppose safe arrival from <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> can be achieved in at most <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> steps. If it can be achieved in at most <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> steps, then <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}\subseteq\mathcal{R}_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{n}\subseteq\mathcal{R}_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Otherwise, the first step is taken from a state in <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and some first action <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> leads to a successor from which safe arrival can be achieved in at most <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> steps. By the induction hypothesis, this successor lies in <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A4.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{n=0}^{\infty}\mathcal{R}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{n=0}^{\infty}\mathcal{R}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the set of states with finite minimum safe arrival time. This set is also <math id="A4.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the definition of the optimal undiscounted value. The identity (<a href="#A4.E63" title="In Proposition D.3 (Finite-step characterization of the safe-arrival region). ‣ D.1 Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>) follows from the same induction argument and the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Discounted Safe-Arrival Value</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now define the discounted Safe-Arrival Value. The discounted value retains the same first-arrival structure as the undiscounted one, while assigning larger value to earlier safe arrival at the base set.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a discount factor <math id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For a deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u):=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u):=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The associated state-value function is</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x):=Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,\pi(x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x):=Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,\pi(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The discounted sum pays only at the first safe arrival time. This gives both a hitting-time interpretation and a random-horizon interpretation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Interpretations of Discounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmproposition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, let <math id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of the controlled rollout and satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{N}(N=k)=(1-\beta)\beta^{k},\qquad k=0,1,2,\ldots." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{N}(N=k)=(1-\beta)\beta^{k},\qquad k=0,1,2,\ldots.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\left(\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}\otimes\mathbb{P}_{N}\right)\left(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}\leq N\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\left(\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}\otimes\mathbb{P}_{N}\right)\left(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}\leq N\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{\beta}:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{\beta}:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The same pathwise argument used in the proof of Proposition <a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1 (Indicator Representation of Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.1 Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> shows that, on the event <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the only nonzero term in <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs at <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\tau_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\tau_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and its value is <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Outside this event, all terms vanish. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{\beta}=\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{\beta}=\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation proves (<a href="#A4.E66" title="In Proposition D.4 (Interpretations of Discounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the random-horizon identity, note that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{N}(N\geq k)=\sum_{n=k}^{\infty}(1-\beta)\beta^{n}=\beta^{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{N}(N\geq k)=\sum_{n=k}^{\infty}(1-\beta)\beta^{n}=\beta^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By independence of <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and the controlled rollout,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}\otimes\mathbb{P}_{N}\right)\left(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}\leq N\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}\otimes\mathbb{P}_{N}\right)\left(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}\leq N\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=k&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}})\,\mathbb{P}_{N}(N\geq k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=k&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}})\,\mathbb{P}_{N}(N\geq k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=k&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\mathbb{P}_{x,u}^{\pi}(\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=k&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\beta^{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}},\ \tau_{\mathcal{B}}&lt;\infty\}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this identity with (<a href="#A4.E66" title="In Proposition D.4 (Interpretations of Discounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>) proves (<a href="#A4.E68" title="In Proposition D.4 (Interpretations of Discounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The discounted value satisfies the following one-step self-consistency relation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Self-Consistency Condition of Discounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmproposition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A4.Thmproposition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\,Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}\!\left(F(x,u),\pi(F(x,u))\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\,Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}\!\left(F(x,u),\pi(F(x,u))\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Starting from (<a href="#A4.E64" title="In Definition D.4 (Discounted Safe-Arrival Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\mathbf{b}(x_{0})+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\mathbf{b}(x_{0})+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\beta^{k}\left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\beta^{k-1}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\beta^{k-1}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{k-1}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{k})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Re-indexing with <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=k-1</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\beta^{j}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\beta^{j}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{+}=F(x,u)=x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{+}=F(x,u)=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The shifted rollout from step <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> onward is the rollout initialized at <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{+},\pi(x^{+}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{+},\pi(x^{+}))</annotation></semantics></math> under the same policy <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\beta^{j}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right]=Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x^{+},\pi(x^{+}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,u}^{\pi}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\beta^{j}\left(\prod_{i=1}^{j}\mathbf{c}(x_{i})\right)\mathbf{b}(x_{j+1})\right]=Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x^{+},\pi(x^{+})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{+}=F(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{+}=F(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math> proves the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Define the optimal discounted values by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u):=\sup_{\pi}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u),\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x):=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>π</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u):=\sup_{\pi}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u),\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x):=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">The corresponding Bellman equation is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}\!\left(F(x,u),u^{+}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}\!\left(F(x,u),u^{+}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left[\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(F(x,u))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=\max_{u\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left[\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(F(x,u))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The discounted Bellman operator</p>
<table id="A4.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\mathcal{T}_{\beta}Q)(x,u):=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q(F(x,u),u^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\mathcal{T}_{\beta}Q)(x,u):=\mathbf{b}(x)+\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}Q(F(x,u),u^{+})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">is a <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-contraction in the sup norm. Indeed, for any two bounded action-value functions <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{1},Q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{1},Q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|(\mathcal{T}_{\beta}Q_{1})(x,u)-(\mathcal{T}_{\beta}Q_{2})(x,u)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|(\mathcal{T}_{\beta}Q_{1})(x,u)-(\mathcal{T}_{\beta}Q_{2})(x,u)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left|Q_{1}(F(x,u),u^{+})-Q_{2}(F(x,u),u^{+})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\beta\,\mathbf{c}(x)\max_{u^{+}\in{\mathcal{U}}}\left|Q_{1}(F(x,u),u^{+})-Q_{2}(F(x,u),u^{+})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\beta\|Q_{1}-Q_{2}\|_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\beta\|Q_{1}-Q_{2}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the discounted Bellman equation has a unique bounded fixed point, namely <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The discounted and undiscounted fixed-policy values have the same success support.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.6</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discounting Preserves Safe-Arrival Feasibility)<span id="A4.Thmproposition6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every deterministic policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, every <math id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and every <math id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\beta\uparrow 1}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\beta\uparrow 1}Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the rollout is deterministic, either the safe-arrival event occurs or it does not. If it occurs, then <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=N</annotation></semantics></math> for some finite <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=1,\qquad Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\beta^{N}&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\pi}(x,u)=1,\qquad Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\pi}(x,u)=\beta^{N}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">If it does not occur, then both values are zero. This proves (<a href="#A4.E86" title="In Proposition D.6 (Discounting Preserves Safe-Arrival Feasibility). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>). The limit (<a href="#A4.E87" title="In Proposition D.6 (Discounting Preserves Safe-Arrival Feasibility). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>) follows from <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{N}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{N}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\uparrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\uparrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> for every finite <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The next proposition gives the precise time-optimal implication of discounting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.7</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value)<span id="A4.Thmproposition7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=\begin{cases}\beta^{d(x)},&amp;d(x)&lt;\infty,\\
0,&amp;d(x)=\infty.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=\begin{cases}\beta^{d(x)},&amp;d(x)&lt;\infty,\\
0,&amp;d(x)=\infty.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for every <math id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,u)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;x\in{\mathcal{B}},\\
\beta^{1+d(F(x,u))},&amp;x\in{\mathcal{H}}\ \text{and}\ d(F(x,u))&lt;\infty,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;x\in{\mathcal{B}},\\
\beta^{1+d(F(x,u))},&amp;x\in{\mathcal{H}}\ \text{and}\ d(F(x,u))&lt;\infty,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, for every <math id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1\}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:d(x)&lt;\infty\}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)&gt;0\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1\}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:d(x)&lt;\infty\}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)&gt;0\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition7.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\beta\uparrow 1}V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\beta\uparrow 1}V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under deterministic dynamics and a deterministic policy, either the trajectory arrives at <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> before <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> in exactly <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps for some finite <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, or the safe-arrival event does not occur. In the first case, the discounted value is <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>; in the second case, it is zero. Since <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, maximizing the discounted value among successful policies is equivalent to minimizing the number of steps required for safe arrival. The minimum such number is <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence (<a href="#A4.E89" title="In Proposition D.7 (Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">89</span></a>) holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">The action-value expression (<a href="#A4.E90" title="In Proposition D.7 (Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">90</span></a>) follows by separating the first action. If <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, safe arrival has already occurred at time <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the value is <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, failure has already occurred at time <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the value is <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, taking action <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> first moves the system to <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x,u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Safe arrival remains possible exactly when <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(F(x,u))&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(F(x,u))&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case the shortest safe arrival time after taking <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+d(F(x,u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+d(F(x,u))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The equivalence (<a href="#A4.E91" title="In Proposition D.7 (Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">91</span></a>) follows from (<a href="#A4.E89" title="In Proposition D.7 (Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">89</span></a>) and the definition of <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, if <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{d(x)}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{d(x)}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\uparrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\uparrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.SS2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves (<a href="#A4.E92" title="In Proposition D.7 (Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">92</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Behavior of Optimal Safe-Arrival Actions</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding results imply a complete qualitative description of optimal safe-arrival actions across the state space. The relevant state-space partition is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{X}}={\mathcal{B}}\,\dot{\cup}\,{\mathcal{F}}\,\dot{\cup}\,(\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\cap{\mathcal{H}})\,\dot{\cup}\,({\mathcal{H}}\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∪</mo><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∪</mo><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∪</mo><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{X}}={\mathcal{B}}\,\dot{\cup}\,{\mathcal{F}}\,\dot{\cup}\,(\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\cap{\mathcal{H}})\,\dot{\cup}\,({\mathcal{H}}\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.8</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Qualitative Structure of Optimal Safe-Arrival Actions)<span id="A4.Thmproposition8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The optimal safe-arrival values and actions satisfy the following four cases.</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1,\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1,\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Every action has the same value, because safe arrival has already occurred at time </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=0,\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=0,\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Every action has the same value, because failure has already occurred at time </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\cap{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\cap{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then an action </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is optimal for the undiscounted optimal action-value if and only if</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Equivalently,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus an undiscounted optimal first action preserves safe-arrival feasibility. A complete policy must still select future actions so that </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is reached in finite time; the undiscounted criterion does not distinguish among successful policies with different arrival times.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the discounted criterion,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)=\begin{cases}\beta^{1+d(F(x,u))},&amp;F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}},\\
0,&amp;F(x,u)\notin\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x,u)=\begin{cases}\beta^{1+d(F(x,u))},&amp;F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}},\\
0,&amp;F(x,u)\notin\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hence </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is discounted-optimal at </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\qquad\text{and}\qquad d(F(x,u))=d(x)-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\qquad\text{and}\qquad d(F(x,u))=d(x)-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Therefore a discounted optimal policy decreases the minimum safe arrival time by one at every pre-arrival step and reaches </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in exactly </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p2.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> steps.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{H}}\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{H}}\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=0,\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=0,\qquad V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">No policy can safely arrive at </span><math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> from such a state. Hence every action has value zero under the safe-arrival objectives unless an additional secondary criterion is imposed.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=0&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{B}}=0&lt;\tau_{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so both the undiscounted and discounted optimal values equal <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, independently of the chosen action. If <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{F}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{F}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the safe-arrival event cannot occur, and both values equal <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\cap{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}\cap{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore an action <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal for the undiscounted objective exactly when <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#A4.E56" title="In D.1 Undiscounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>), and since <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(F(x,u))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(F(x,u)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x,u)=1</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x,u)\in\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The discounted action-value expression (<a href="#A4.E98" title="In item 3. ‣ Proposition D.8 (Qualitative Structure of Optimal Safe-Arrival Actions). ‣ D.3 Behavior of Optimal Safe-Arrival Actions ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">98</span></a>) follows from (<a href="#A4.E90" title="In Proposition D.7 (Arrival-Time Optimality of the Discounted Value). ‣ D.2 Discounted Safe-Arrival Value ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">90</span></a>). Since <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, maximizing <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{1+d(F(x,u))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{1+d(F(x,u))}</annotation></semantics></math> over feasible successors is equivalent to minimizing <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(F(x,u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(F(x,u))</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimum feasible successor distance is <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is discounted-optimal if and only if (<a href="#A4.E99" title="In item 3. ‣ Proposition D.8 (Qualitative Structure of Optimal Safe-Arrival Actions). ‣ D.3 Behavior of Optimal Safe-Arrival Actions ‣ Appendix D Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">99</span></a>) holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, if <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{H}}\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{H}}\setminus\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x)=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x)=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence no policy can safely arrive at <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, so both the undiscounted and discounted optimal values are zero. This proves the final case.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Roles of Undiscounted and Discounted Safe-Arrival Value)<span id="A4.Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The undiscounted safe-arrival value defines the safe-arrival specification and the feasible safe-arrival region</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x)=1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The discounted safe-arrival value preserves this region,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)&gt;0\},\qquad\beta\in(0,1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{SA}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:V_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{\star}(x)&gt;0\},\qquad\beta\in(0,1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and further ranks successful policies according to their arrival time. Thus the undiscounted value provides the feasibility semantics, while the discounted value provides a contraction-based, time-sensitive objective for RL training.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>PS2-RL Details and Proofs</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Base Set Certification Proof</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Existence of a Certified Local Base Set). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#S4.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 4.1 (Local Stabilizability). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(b), there exists <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A-BK" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-BK</annotation></semantics></math> is Hurwitz. Fix any such <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Lyapunov equation for stable linear systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, Thm 4.6]</cite>, there exists a unique <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(A-BK)^{\top}P+P(A-BK)=-Q." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(A-BK)^{\top}P+P(A-BK)=-Q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define the error coordinate <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e:=x-x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e:=x-x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and the candidate Lyapunov function as</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V(e)=e^{\top}Pe." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V(e)=e^{\top}Pe.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The closed-loop nonlinear dynamics under <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}=f(x)+g(x)(u^{\star}-K(x-x^{\star}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}=f(x)+g(x)(u^{\star}-K(x-x^{\star}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(e):=f(x^{\star}+e)+g(x^{\star}+e)(u^{\star}-Ke)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(e):=f(x^{\star}+e)+g(x^{\star}+e)(u^{\star}-Ke)</annotation></semantics></math>, a Taylor expansion of <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=0</annotation></semantics></math> combined with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(0)=f(x^{\star})+g(x^{\star})u^{\star}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(0)=f(x^{\star})+g(x^{\star})u^{\star}=0</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#S4.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 4.1 (Local Stabilizability). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(a)) gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{e}\;=\;F(e)\;=\;(A-BK)\,e\,+\,\rho(e),\qquad\|\rho(e)\|=o(\|e\|)\text{ as }e\to 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{e}\;=\;F(e)\;=\;(A-BK)\,e\,+\,\rho(e),\qquad\|\rho(e)\|=o(\|e\|)\text{ as }e\to 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the remainder <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> inherits the smoothness of <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using (<a href="#A5.E104" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 Base Set Certification Proof ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E105" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 Base Set Certification Proof ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">105</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{V}(e)\;=\;2\,e^{\top}P\,\dot{e}\;=\;-\,e^{\top}Q\,e\;+\;\underbrace{2\,e^{\top}P\,\rho(e)}_{=:\,R(e)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{V}(e)\;=\;2\,e^{\top}P\,\dot{e}\;=\;-\,e^{\top}Q\,e\;+\;\underbrace{2\,e^{\top}P\,\rho(e)}_{=:\,R(e)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R(e)|\leq 2\|P\|\,\|e\|\,\|\rho(e)\|=o(\|e\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R(e)|\leq 2\|P\|\,\|e\|\,\|\rho(e)\|=o(\|e\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence there exists <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\|e\|\leq r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\|e\|\leq r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{V}(e)\;\leq\;-\tfrac{1}{2}\lambda_{\min}(Q)\,\|e\|^{2}\;&lt;\;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{V}(e)\;\leq\;-\tfrac{1}{2}\lambda_{\min}(Q)\,\|e\|^{2}\;&lt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}:=\lambda_{\min}(P)\,r_{1}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}:=\lambda_{\min}(P)\,r_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e:V(e)\leq c_{1}\}\subseteq\{e:\|e\|\leq r_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e:V(e)\leq c_{1}\}\subseteq\{e:\|e\|\leq r_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V}(e)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V}(e)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{0&lt;V(e)\leq c_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0&lt;V(e)\leq c_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, establishing Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Existence of a Certified Local Base Set). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(c) and (d) for any <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by the standard Lyapunov invariance theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, Thm. 4.1]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to shrink <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> so that Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Existence of a Certified Local Base Set). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>(a) and (b) also hold. Since <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}\in\mathrm{int}({\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}\in\mathrm{int}({\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:h_{\mathcal{S}}(x)\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:h_{\mathcal{S}}(x)\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero-superlevel set of the continuous function <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}_{c_{2}}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}_{c_{2}}\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Analogously, since <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\star}\in\mathrm{int}({\mathcal{U}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\star}\in\mathrm{int}({\mathcal{U}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, and the map <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{B}}(x)=u^{\star}-K(x-x^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{B}}(x)=u^{\star}-K(x-x^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, there exists <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{B}}({\mathcal{B}}_{c_{3}})\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{B}}({\mathcal{B}}_{c_{3}})\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{c}\;:=\;\min\{c_{1},c_{2},c_{3}\}\;&gt;\;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{c}\;:=\;\min\{c_{1},c_{2},c_{3}\}\;&gt;\;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">yields all four properties simultaneously for every <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,\bar{c}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,\bar{c}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>PS2-RL Decomposition Proof</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2 (Certified Decomposition and Exactness of PS2-RL). ‣ 4.1.3 Certified decomposition guarantee ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove (i). Let <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in{\mathcal{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in{\mathcal{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Subproblem <a href="#Thmsubproblem2" title="Subproblem 2 (Safe-Arrival Set Maximization). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}_{0}\subseteq{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}_{0}\subseteq{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The set
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero-superlevel set of the implicit BCBF</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{{\mathcal{C}_{T}}}(x)=\min\left\{\min_{{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T]}h_{\mathcal{S}}(\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})),\;h_{\mathcal{B}}(\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,T))\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{{\mathcal{C}_{T}}}(x)=\min\left\{\min_{{t^{\prime}}\in[0,T]}h_{\mathcal{S}}(\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,{t^{\prime}})),\;h_{\mathcal{B}}(\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,T))\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By construction of <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>, every action
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\pi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\pi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the pointwise BCBF
inequalities on the backup rollout and the terminal base-set condition.
These pointwise inequalities are a sufficient condition for the CBF condition
on <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\mathcal{C}_{T}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\mathcal{C}_{T}}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, Prop. 2]</cite>. Therefore <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math> is
forward invariant under any policy in <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting trajectory satisfies
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\pi}(t;x_{0})\in{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\pi}(t;x_{0})\in{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> by definition, so the executed input
also satisfies the actuator constraint. Hence
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})\subseteq\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})\subseteq\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Statement (ii) follows directly from the definition of
<math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a solution of Subproblem <a href="#Thmsubproblem1" title="Subproblem 1 (BCBF-Constrained Policy Optimization). ‣ BCBF-admissible input set. ‣ 4.1.1 BCBF-constrained policies under a fixed backup policy ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Since
Subproblem <a href="#Thmsubproblem1" title="Subproblem 1 (BCBF-Constrained Policy Optimization). ‣ BCBF-admissible input set. ‣ 4.1.1 BCBF-constrained policies under a fixed backup policy ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> optimizes <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> over
<math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})=\sup_{\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})}J(\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})=\sup_{\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})}J(\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The inequality</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})}J(\pi)\quad\leq\quad\sup_{\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}}J(\pi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})}J(\pi)\quad\leq\quad\sup_{\pi\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}}J(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">then follows from part (i).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, suppose there exists a globally optimal safe policy
<math id="A5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}}\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>safe</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}}\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})\geq J(\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>safe</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})\geq J(\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">But by part (i), <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>safe</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is globally optimal over <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathrm{safe}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})\leq J(\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>safe</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})\leq J(\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})=J(\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>safe</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J({\pi_{\phi}^{\star}})=J(\pi^{\star}_{{\mathrm{safe}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, proving that
<math id="A5.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> is globally optimal for Problem <a href="#Thmproblem1" title="Problem 1 (PS2-RL Formulation). ‣ 3 Problem Formulation ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>PS2-RL Safety Guarantee Proof</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Safety Guarantee of PS2-RL). ‣ 4.4 Phase II: Training with the Control-Invariant Layer ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the control-invariant layer returns the projection of <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\phi}_{\mathrm{PS2}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})\qquad\forall x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>PS2</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\phi}_{\mathrm{PS2}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})\in{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})\qquad\forall x\in{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly the defining property of <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\phi}_{\mathrm{PS2}}\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>PS2</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\phi}_{\mathrm{PS2}}\in\Pi_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The conclusion then follows immediately from Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2 (Certified Decomposition and Exactness of PS2-RL). ‣ 4.1.3 Certified decomposition guarantee ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>PS2-RL Universal Approximation Proof</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4 (Universal Approximation of PS2-RL). ‣ 4.4 Phase II: Training with the Control-Invariant Layer ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega\subseteq{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega\subseteq{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math> is nonempty by BCBF feasibility and convex because <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex and the BCBF constraints are affine in <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> under the fixed backup flow.
Thus (<a href="#S4.E13" title="In Definition 4.2 (Control-Invariant Layer). ‣ 4.4 Phase II: Training with the Control-Invariant Layer ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is precisely a <span id="A5.SS4.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HardNet-CVX</span> projection with state-dependent convex feasible set <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The result follows directly from the universal-approximation theorem for <span id="A5.SS4.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HardNet-CVX</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, Thm. 12]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.5 </span>Constructing the CIL from Differentiable Simulators</h3>

<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As briefly discussed in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Scalability of PS2-RL ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>, PS2-RL does not fundamentally require a hand-derived symbolic decomposition <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)+g(x)u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)+g(x)u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose instead that a differentiable simulator <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{{\Delta t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{{\Delta t}}</annotation></semantics></math> is available. For a fixed backup policy, define the candidate-control-input rollout</p>
<table id="A5.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{0}(u)=F_{{\Delta t}}(x,u),\qquad z_{i+1}(u)=F_{{\Delta t}}\bigl(z_{i}(u),{\pi_{b}^{\star}}(z_{i}(u))\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{0}(u)=F_{{\Delta t}}(x,u),\qquad z_{i+1}(u)=F_{{\Delta t}}\bigl(z_{i}(u),{\pi_{b}^{\star}}(z_{i}(u))\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For each backup rollout condition <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(z_{i}(u))\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(z_{i}(u))\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to either a sampled safe-set condition or the terminal base-set condition, automatic differentiation gives</p>
<table id="A5.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{i}(x)=\nabla_{u}\ell_{i}(z_{i}(u))\big|_{u=u_{b}},\qquad u_{b}={\pi_{b}^{\star}}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{i}(x)=\nabla_{u}\ell_{i}(z_{i}(u))\big|_{u=u_{b}},\qquad u_{b}={\pi_{b}^{\star}}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and hence the local affine row</p>
<table id="A5.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{i}(z_{i}(u_{b}))+a_{i}(x)^{\top}(u-u_{b})\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{i}(z_{i}(u_{b}))+a_{i}(x)^{\top}(u-u_{b})\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">These simulator-generated rows can be inserted into the same control-invariant layer.
For high-dimensional simulators, one need not materialize the full state sensitivity matrix, as vector–Jacobian products or reduced sensitivities for only the constraint-relevant outputs are sufficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This simulator-based variant should be interpreted as a discrete-time, locally affine realization of PS2-RL.
With an exact control-affine model, the rows in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In BCBF-admissible input set. ‣ 4.1.1 BCBF-constrained policies under a fixed backup policy ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) are exact and the guarantees in Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Safety Guarantee of PS2-RL). ‣ 4.4 Phase II: Training with the Control-Invariant Layer ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> apply directly.
With a general differentiable simulator, the local rows are first-order approximations, and in that case one can add conservative margins or impose a trust region around <math id="A5.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the main scaling bottleneck is not closed-form dynamics or explicit invariant-set synthesis, but access to a differentiable rollout model whose accuracy is sufficient over the backup horizon.
Employing PS2-RL with a differentiable simulator, without the analytical dynamics, is left as future work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14536v1/Framework_Tix.svg" id="A5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:381/334;" width="381" height="334"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Block-diagram view of the two-phase PS2-RL framework, complementing Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
<span id="A5.F4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase I (top)</span>: the safe-arrival policy <math id="A5.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is trained against the environment using the indicators <math id="A5.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x_{k}),\mathbf{f}(x_{k}),\mathbf{c}(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x_{k}),\mathbf{f}(x_{k}),\mathbf{c}(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A5.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}},{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}},{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the continuation set, optimizing the discounted safe-arrival value Bellman recursion.
<span id="A5.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase II (bottom)</span>: the composed backup policy <math id="A5.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{b}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{b}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is frozen and used to construct the BCBF-admissible set online for each timestep. The control value from the RL policy <math id="A5.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math> is projected onto this set by the control-invariant layer (a differentiable QP), and task-reward gradients propagate end-to-end through the projection back into <math id="A5.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6 </span>Phase I: Safe-Arrival Policy Training</h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we expand on Phase I beyond the high-level description in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Phase I: Training the Safe-Arrival Policy ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
Phase I addresses Subproblem <a href="#Thmsubproblem2" title="Subproblem 2 (Safe-Arrival Set Maximization). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> by learning a parameterized safe-arrival policy <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> that enlarges the backup-induced control-invariant set <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math>, given the certified base pair <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{B}},\pi_{\mathcal{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{B}},\pi_{\mathcal{B}})</annotation></semantics></math> from Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Existence of a Certified Local Base Set). ‣ Certified base set and base controller. ‣ 4.1.2 Learning the safe-arrival policy to enlarge the implicit invariant set ‣ 4.1 Decomposing Safety and Performance from Problem ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
Fig. <a href="#A5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ E.5 Constructing the CIL from Differentiable Simulators ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (top) summarizes the resulting training loop: the policy interacts with the environment, stepwise indicators of <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the continuation set are recorded along each rollout, and the parameters are updated with the discounted safe-arrival value Bellman recursion (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2 Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Safe-Arrival Policy Training</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            sampler <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>arr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, dynamics <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, sets <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, discount <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Initialize safe-arrival policy parameters <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and value/Q-function parameters

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> not converged <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Sample initial states <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\sim\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>arr</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\sim\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Collect rollouts under <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> until <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}\in{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}\in{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}\in{\mathcal{F}}={\mathcal{X}}\setminus{\mathcal{S}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}\in{\mathcal{F}}={\mathcal{X}}\setminus{\mathcal{S}},</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              For each <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, assign indicators <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}(x_{k}),\,\mathbf{f}(x_{k})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}(x_{k}),\,\mathbf{f}(x_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}(x_{k})=1-\mathbf{b}(x_{k})-\mathbf{f}(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}(x_{k})=1-\mathbf{b}(x_{k})-\mathbf{f}(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              Update the chosen value/Q estimator using the safe-arrival value Bellman recursion (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2 Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              Improve <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> with the chosen RL backbone

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and freeze the composed <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> for Phase II

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Phase I objective can be written as</p>
<table id="A5.E106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\theta}\;J_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}}\!\left[Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}}(x,{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}(x))\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>arr</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\theta}\;J_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}}\!\left[Q_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}^{{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}}(x,{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}(x))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ E.6 Phase I: Safe-Arrival Policy Training ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes Phase I at the framework level.
In practice, one can take <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega={\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega={\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, or a smaller design region of interest inside <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>arr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}</annotation></semantics></math> to focus training on the portion of state space from which safe arrival is desired.
Details on <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>arr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each experiment are provided in App. <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 PS2-RL Implementation Details ‣ Appendix F Experiment Details ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>.
The only safe-arrival policy-specific ingredients are the indicators <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b},\mathbf{f},\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b},\mathbf{f},\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, first-hit termination at <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the objective function with the safe-arrival value.
Everything else can be supplied by a chosen RL backbone, such as actor-critic, Q-learning, fitted value iteration, and related methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.7 </span>Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy</h3>

<div id="A5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix expands the control-invariant layer construction and PS2-RL policy training in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Phase II: Training with the Control-Invariant Layer ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, which corresponds to the bottom panel of Fig. <a href="#A5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ E.5 Constructing the CIL from Differentiable Simulators ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
The main text defines the control-invariant layer as the projection of a nominal policy output onto the BCBF-admissible set <math id="A5.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{K}}_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕂</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{K}}_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x;{\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, we write the finite-mesh QP explicitly in the standard affine form and describe the differentiable solver used in implementation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.7.1 </span>Control-Invariant Layer Construction and Solver</h4>

<section id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Construction of the BCBF-admissible input set.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For this subsection, we allow the safe set and base set to be defined by multiple differentiable inequalities,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E107.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x)\geq 0,\;j=1,\ldots,n_{{\mathcal{S}}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x)\geq 0,\;j=1,\ldots,n_{{\mathcal{S}}}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E108.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x)\geq 0,\;\ell=1,\ldots,n_{{\mathcal{B}}}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x)\geq 0,\;\ell=1,\ldots,n_{{\mathcal{B}}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The scalar case used in the main text is recovered by setting <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{{\mathcal{S}}}=n_{{\mathcal{B}}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{{\mathcal{S}}}=n_{{\mathcal{B}}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let the finite backup mesh be <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=t^{\prime}_{0}&lt;t^{\prime}_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;t^{\prime}_{N}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=t^{\prime}_{0}&lt;t^{\prime}_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;t^{\prime}_{N}=T</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a fixed state <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and the frozen backup policy <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A5.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}^{b}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}^{b}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,t^{\prime}_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,t^{\prime}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E109.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E109.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\Psi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,t^{\prime}_{i})=\frac{\partial\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,t^{\prime}_{i})}{\partial x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\Psi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,t^{\prime}_{i})=\frac{\partial\Phi_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}(x,t^{\prime}_{i})}{\partial x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E109.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{i}^{b}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{i}^{b}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E109.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=f_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}\!\left(x_{i}^{b}(x)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=f_{{\pi_{b}^{\star}}}\!\left(x_{i}^{b}(x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The current-state control-affine terms are denoted by <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}:=f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}:=f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{0}:=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{0}:=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For every safety constraint component <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}</annotation></semantics></math> and backup node <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the BCBF rollout condition is</p>
<table id="A5.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})^{\top}\Big[\Psi_{i}(x)\big(f_{0}+g_{0}u\big)-f_{i}^{b}(x)\Big]+\alpha_{{\mathcal{S}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})\right)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})^{\top}\Big[\Psi_{i}(x)\big(f_{0}+g_{0}u\big)-f_{i}^{b}(x)\Big]+\alpha_{{\mathcal{S}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})\right)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, this is an affine inequality in the current input <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)^{\top}u\leq b^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)^{\top}u\leq b^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="A5.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E112.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=-\nabla h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{i}(x)g_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=-\nabla h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{i}(x)g_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{{\mathcal{S}}}_{i,j}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E113.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\alpha_{{\mathcal{S}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})\right)+\nabla h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})^{\top}\Big[\Psi_{i}(x)f_{0}-f_{i}^{b}(x)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\alpha_{{\mathcal{S}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})\right)+\nabla h_{{\mathcal{S}},j}(x_{i}^{b})^{\top}\Big[\Psi_{i}(x)f_{0}-f_{i}^{b}(x)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At the terminal node <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=t^{\prime}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=t^{\prime}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, each base-set constraint component gives</p>
<table id="A5.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{N}(x)\big(f_{0}+g_{0}u\big)+\alpha_{{\mathcal{B}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})\right)\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{N}(x)\big(f_{0}+g_{0}u\big)+\alpha_{{\mathcal{B}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})\right)\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">or equivalently</p>
<table id="A5.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)^{\top}u\leq b^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)^{\top}u\leq b^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A5.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E116.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=-\nabla h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{N}(x)g_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=-\nabla h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{N}(x)g_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{{\mathcal{B}}}_{\ell}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E117.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\alpha_{{\mathcal{B}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})\right)+\nabla h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{N}(x)f_{0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\alpha_{{\mathcal{B}}}\!\left(h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})\right)+\nabla h_{{\mathcal{B}},\ell}(x_{N}^{b})^{\top}\Psi_{N}(x)f_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Stacking all safety rows and terminal rows gives</p>
<table id="A5.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E118.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\begin{bmatrix}A_{{\mathcal{S}}}(x)\\
A_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x)\end{bmatrix}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n_{c}\times m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\begin{bmatrix}A_{{\mathcal{S}}}(x)\\
A_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x)\end{bmatrix}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n_{c}\times m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E118.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E118.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\begin{bmatrix}b_{{\mathcal{S}}}(x)\\
b_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x)\end{bmatrix}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n_{c}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\begin{bmatrix}b_{{\mathcal{S}}}(x)\\
b_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x)\end{bmatrix}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n_{c}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{c}=(N+1)n_{{\mathcal{S}}}+n_{{\mathcal{B}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{c}=(N+1)n_{{\mathcal{S}}}+n_{{\mathcal{B}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the finite-mesh BCBF constraints can be written compactly as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)u\leq b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)u\leq b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">For a boxed input limit set</p>
<table id="A5.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{U}}=\{u\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}:u_{\min}\leq u\leq u_{\max}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{U}}=\{u\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}:u_{\min}\leq u\leq u_{\max}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">the actuator constraints are</p>
<table id="A5.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}},\qquad A_{{\mathcal{U}}}:=\begin{bmatrix}I_{m}\\
-I_{m}\end{bmatrix},\qquad b_{{\mathcal{U}}}:=\begin{bmatrix}u_{\max}\\
-u_{\min}\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}},\qquad A_{{\mathcal{U}}}:=\begin{bmatrix}I_{m}\\
-I_{m}\end{bmatrix},\qquad b_{{\mathcal{U}}}:=\begin{bmatrix}u_{\max}\\
-u_{\min}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Then, the control-invariant layer is a quadratic program:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}({\pi_{\phi}})(x)=\argmin_{u}\|u-{\pi_{\phi}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}\\
&amp;\mathrm{s.t.}\quad A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)u\leq b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x),\;\;A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>CIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.007em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}({\pi_{\phi}})(x)=\argmin_{u}\|u-{\pi_{\phi}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}\\
&amp;\mathrm{s.t.}\quad A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)u\leq b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x),\;\;A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Slack-regularized QP.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In implementation, we solve a slack-regularized version of (<a href="#A5.E122" title="In Construction of the BCBF-admissible input set. ‣ E.7.1 Control-Invariant Layer Construction and Solver ‣ E.7 Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">122</span></a>).
Specifically, the QP decision variable is <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=[u^{\top},\delta]^{\top}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=[u^{\top},\delta]^{\top}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar slack shared across all BCBF rows:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;(u^{\star},\delta^{\star})=\argmin_{u,\delta}\|u-{\pi_{\phi}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda_{\delta}\delta^{2}\\
&amp;\mathrm{s.t.}\quad A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)u-\mathbf{1}_{n_{c}}\delta\leq b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x),\quad A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}},\quad\delta\geq 0,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;(u^{\star},\delta^{\star})=\argmin_{u,\delta}\|u-{\pi_{\phi}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda_{\delta}\delta^{2}\\
&amp;\mathrm{s.t.}\quad A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)u-\mathbf{1}_{n_{c}}\delta\leq b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x),\quad A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}},\quad\delta\geq 0,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\delta}\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\delta}\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
In our experiments, <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\delta,\mathrm{unicycle}}=10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>unicycle</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\delta,\mathrm{unicycle}}=10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\delta,\mathrm{quadrotor}}=10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>quadrotor</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\delta,\mathrm{quadrotor}}=10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the control-invariant layer returns only the control component,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}^{\lambda_{\delta}}({\pi_{\phi}})(x):=u^{\star}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>CIL</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}^{\lambda_{\delta}}({\pi_{\phi}})(x):=u^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The slack variable is included for numerical robustness.
The exact BCBF theory is continuous-time, while the implemented layer uses a finite backup mesh, numerical integration of the backup flow and sensitivity, and a sampled-data controller whose action is held by ZOH.
Near the boundary of <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>, these approximations can create small artificial infeasibilities even when the ideal continuous-time BCBF condition is feasible.
A heavily penalized slack prevents such numerical infeasibilities from causing solver failure or unstable gradients.
The slack relaxes only the BCBF rows, not the control limits <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{{\mathcal{U}}}u\leq b_{{\mathcal{U}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus every executed control still satisfies <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\star}\in{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\star}\in{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The zero-slack case <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\star}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\star}=0</annotation></semantics></math> recovers the hard BCBF constraints in (<a href="#A5.E119" title="In Construction of the BCBF-admissible input set. ‣ E.7.1 Control-Invariant Layer Construction and Solver ‣ E.7 Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">119</span></a>), and the formal safety guarantees in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Phase II: Training with the Control-Invariant Layer ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> correspond to this exact hard-constraint setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Slack-regularized QP. ‣ E.7.1 Control-Invariant Layer Construction and Solver ‣ E.7 Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> confirms that <em id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">the slack-regularized control-invariant layer is effectively operating in the hard-constraint regime throughout evaluation</em>.
Across both environments and both PS2-RL variants, the mean and median slack values are on the order of <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> or smaller, and even the 99th percentile remains at most <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.10\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.10\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, steps with <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> never occur in the unicycle evaluations and occur only rarely in the quadrotor evaluations, even for the more aggressive learned variant.
Thus, the slack term mainly absorbs small numerical discrepancies from finite-mesh backup integration and sampled-data implementation, rather than serving as a meaningful relaxation of the BCBF constraints.
Consistent with this interpretation, the PS2-RL variants retain the <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\%</annotation></semantics></math> safety and strong tracking performance reported in the main experimental Tables <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 Unicycle: Lane-Keeping ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Quadrotor: Powerloop Maneuver ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Control-invariant layer’s slack value during evaluation. For each PS2-RL variant and task, we aggregate the scalar QP slack <math id="A5.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> over all control-invariant layer solves from 10 seeds and 1,000 evaluation episodes per seed.
We report the mean, median, 99th percentile, and fraction of steps with <math id="A5.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Across both tasks, the slack remains near <math id="A5.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> and large slack values are extremely rare, indicating that the relaxation acts primarily as a numerical safeguard rather than an active softening of the BCBF constraints.</figcaption>
<div id="A5.T7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:35.6pt;vertical-align:-16.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-68.1pt,7.0pt) scale(0.717025479833183,0.717025479833183) ;">
<table id="A5.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="4"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unicycle</span> (Total Steps Each: <math id="A5.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.06\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.06</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.06\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="A5.T7.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="4"><span id="A5.T7.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quadrotor</span> (Total Steps Each: <math id="A5.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.0\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.0\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
