</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Differentiable QP solver.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The optimization problems (<a href="#A5.E122" title="In Construction of the BCBF-admissible input set. ‣ E.7.1 Control-Invariant Layer Construction and Solver ‣ E.7 Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">122</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E123" title="In Slack-regularized QP. ‣ E.7.1 Control-Invariant Layer Construction and Solver ‣ E.7 Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">123</span></a>) are convex QP by construction.
Our implementation solves them with <span id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">qpax</span> from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>.
All quantities used to assemble <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS7.SSS1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>BCBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{{\mathrm{BCBF}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are computed with differentiable JAX operations, including the backup rollout, sensitivity propagation, row construction, and the QP solve.
Consequently, the policy update backpropagates directly through the network without an estimator or a separate surrogate loss.
The differentiable solver provides the corresponding gradient used by the RL optimizer.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.7.2 </span>PS2-RL Policy Training through the Control-Invariant Layer</h4>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Phase II freezes the composed backup policy</p>
<table id="A5.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\pi_{b}^{\star}}(x)=\begin{cases}\pi_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x),&amp;x\in{\mathcal{B}},\\
\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x),&amp;x\notin{\mathcal{B}},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\pi_{b}^{\star}}(x)=\begin{cases}\pi_{{\mathcal{B}}}(x),&amp;x\in{\mathcal{B}},\\
\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\star}(x),&amp;x\notin{\mathcal{B}},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and trains only the nominal task policy <math id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a deterministic actor, the executed PS2 action is</p>
<table id="A5.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{k}=\pi^{\phi}_{\mathrm{PS2}}(x_{k};{\pi_{b}^{\star}}):={\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}({\pi_{\phi}})(x_{k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>PS2</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>CIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{k}=\pi^{\phi}_{\mathrm{PS2}}(x_{k};{\pi_{b}^{\star}}):={\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}({\pi_{\phi}})(x_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For a stochastic actor, the nominal action is first sampled from the policy distribution and the control-invariant layer is then applied deterministically:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}_{k}\sim{\pi_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid x_{k}),\qquad u_{k}={\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}({u_{\mathrm{nom}}}_{k})(x_{k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>CIL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}_{k}\sim{\pi_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid x_{k}),\qquad u_{k}={\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathrm{CIL}}}({u_{\mathrm{nom}}}_{k})(x_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The environment and replay buffer therefore only see projected controls <math id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In our implementation, the actor loss evaluates the critic at the projected action <math id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and target-policy actions in Bellman backups are projected through the same control-invariant layer.
Thus the actor is optimized for task return inside the BCBF-admissible action set.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because the control-invariant layer is differentiable, the actor-gradient path contains the QP solution:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{actor}}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{actor}}}{\partial u^{\star}}\frac{\partial u^{\star}}{\partial{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}}\frac{\partial{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}}{\partial\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>actor</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>actor</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>nom</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{actor}}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{actor}}}{\partial u^{\star}}\frac{\partial u^{\star}}{\partial{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}}\frac{\partial{u_{\mathrm{nom}}}}{\partial\phi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This is the key distinction between PS2-RL and a post-hoc non-differentiable shield: the projection layer is present during both data collection and gradient-based policy improvement.
The resulting policy is therefore trained to produce high-return nominal actions whose projections remain close to the nominal command while satisfying the BCBF-induced constraints.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Unicycle Environment Details</h3>

<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">System dynamics.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the following unicycle dynamics for the lane keeping experiment:</p>
<table id="A6.E125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\dot{y}\\
\dot{v}\\
\dot{\psi}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}v\sin(\psi)\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
1&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}a_{\mathrm{cmd}}\\
r_{\mathrm{cmd}}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>cmd</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cmd</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\dot{y}\\
\dot{v}\\
\dot{\psi}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}v\sin(\psi)\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
1&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}a_{\mathrm{cmd}}\\
r_{\mathrm{cmd}}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the state <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> comprises the lateral position <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, velocity <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and the heading angle <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, with control inputs consisting of acceleration <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\mathrm{cmd}}\in[-5,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\mathrm{cmd}}\in[-5,5]</annotation></semantics></math> m/s<sup id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> and yaw rate <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{cmd}}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{cmd}}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> rad/s.
We implement the continuous-time dynamics in sampled-data form with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> sec.
Moreover, all controllers employ a control frequency of 20 Hz, matching the sampling period.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Safe set.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The safe set is specified as <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:|y|\leq y_{\max},|\psi|\leq\psi_{\max}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:|y|\leq y_{\max},|\psi|\leq\psi_{\max}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\max}=1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\max}=1.8</annotation></semantics></math> m and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\max}=\pi/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\max}=\pi/3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we have four safety constraints:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}h_{{\mathcal{S}},1}(x)=y_{\max}+y,\quad\quad h_{{\mathcal{S}},2}(x)&amp;=y_{\max}-y,\\
h_{{\mathcal{S}},3}(x)=\psi_{\max}+\psi,\quad\quad h_{{\mathcal{S}},4}(x)&amp;=\psi_{\max}-\psi.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="3.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="3.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}h_{{\mathcal{S}},1}(x)=y_{\max}+y,\quad\quad h_{{\mathcal{S}},2}(x)&amp;=y_{\max}-y,\\
h_{{\mathcal{S}},3}(x)=\psi_{\max}+\psi,\quad\quad h_{{\mathcal{S}},4}(x)&amp;=\psi_{\max}-\psi.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the safety specification constrains only the lateral position and heading, since these are the variables directly associated with leaving the lane.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reference trajectory, reward, episode setup.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unicycle task is to track a sinusoidal lane reference</p>
<table id="A6.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)=2.5\sin\!\left(\frac{2\pi t}{10}\right),\qquad v_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)=5," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.243em;" width="1.243em"><mi>sin</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)=2.5\sin\!\left(\frac{2\pi t}{10}\right),\qquad v_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)=5,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with heading reference</p>
<table id="A6.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)=\arcsin\!\left(\frac{\dot{y}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)}{v_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.684em;" width="2.684em"><mi>arcsin</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)=\arcsin\!\left(\frac{\dot{y}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)}{v_{{\mathrm{ref}}}(t)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The reference lasts 20 sec and deliberately violates the lane constraint, since its lateral amplitude <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5</annotation></semantics></math> m exceeds <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\max}=1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\max}=1.8</annotation></semantics></math> m. The trajectory-following reward uses the normalized tracking error for step <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi_{k}=\left[\frac{y_{k}-y_{{\mathrm{ref}},k}}{y_{\max}},\;\;\frac{v_{k}-v_{{\mathrm{ref}},k}}{5},\;\;\frac{\mathrm{wrap}(\psi_{k}-\psi_{{\mathrm{ref}},k})}{\psi_{\max}},\;\;\frac{a_{{\mathrm{cmd}},k}}{a_{\max}},\;\;\frac{r_{{\mathrm{cmd}},k}}{r_{\max}}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>wrap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>cmd</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>cmd</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi_{k}=\left[\frac{y_{k}-y_{{\mathrm{ref}},k}}{y_{\max}},\;\;\frac{v_{k}-v_{{\mathrm{ref}},k}}{5},\;\;\frac{\mathrm{wrap}(\psi_{k}-\psi_{{\mathrm{ref}},k})}{\psi_{\max}},\;\;\frac{a_{{\mathrm{cmd}},k}}{a_{\max}},\;\;\frac{r_{{\mathrm{cmd}},k}}{r_{\max}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the step-wise reward is <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}=-\xi_{k}^{\top}L\xi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}=-\xi_{k}^{\top}L\xi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L={\mathrm{diag}}(50,20,10,0.05,0.05)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L={\mathrm{diag}}(50,20,10,0.05,0.05)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\max}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\max}=5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The reward weights are selected by fine-tuning a vanilla tracking policy trained to follow the reference trajectory without any safety mechanism or safety-aware objective.
That is, these weights were chosen purely for nominal sinewave tracking performance, without safety in mind.
Since the environment uses <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> and the reference is 20 seconds, the episode horizon is 400 steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Quadrotor Environment Details</h3>

<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">System dynamics.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the following quadrotor dynamics for the powerloop tracking experiment:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\dot{\mathbf{p}}=\mathbf{v},\quad\dot{\mathbf{v}}=-g\mathbf{e}_{3}+R(\mathbf{q})({a_{\text{cmd}}}\mathbf{e}_{3})&amp;,\quad\dot{\mathbf{q}}=\frac{1}{2}\Xi(\mathbf{q}){\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}},\\
\Xi(\mathbf{q})=\begin{bmatrix}-q_{x}&amp;-q_{y}&amp;-q_{z}\\
q_{w}&amp;-q_{z}&amp;q_{y}\\
q_{z}&amp;q_{w}&amp;-q_{x}\\
-q_{y}&amp;q_{x}&amp;q_{w}\end{bmatrix}&amp;\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\dot{\mathbf{p}}=\mathbf{v},\quad\dot{\mathbf{v}}=-g\mathbf{e}_{3}+R(\mathbf{q})({a_{\text{cmd}}}\mathbf{e}_{3})&amp;,\quad\dot{\mathbf{q}}=\frac{1}{2}\Xi(\mathbf{q}){\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}},\\
\Xi(\mathbf{q})=\begin{bmatrix}-q_{x}&amp;-q_{y}&amp;-q_{z}\\
q_{w}&amp;-q_{z}&amp;q_{y}\\
q_{z}&amp;q_{w}&amp;-q_{x}\\
-q_{y}&amp;q_{x}&amp;q_{w}\end{bmatrix}&amp;\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is the quaternion kinematic matrix. The state <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=[\mathbf{p}^{\top},\mathbf{v}^{\top},\mathbf{q}^{\top}]^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=[\mathbf{p}^{\top},\mathbf{v}^{\top},\mathbf{q}^{\top}]^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{10}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the inertial position <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=[p_{x},p_{y},p_{z}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=[p_{x},p_{y},p_{z}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inertial linear velocity <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}=[v_{x},v_{y},v_{z}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}=[v_{x},v_{y},v_{z}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the unit quaternion <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}^{\top}=[q_{w},q_{x},q_{y},q_{z}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}^{\top}=[q_{w},q_{x},q_{y},q_{z}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the global, inertial orientation. The control input <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=[{a_{\text{cmd}}},{\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}}^{\top}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>ω</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=[{a_{\text{cmd}}},{\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}}^{\top}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the mass-normalized thrust, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{a_{\text{cmd}}}\in[0,4g]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{a_{\text{cmd}}}\in[0,4g]</annotation></semantics></math>, for gravitational acceleration <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=9.81m/s^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9.81</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=9.81m/s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the body rate, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}}=[\omega_{x},\omega_{y},\omega_{z}]^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext>cmd</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{\omega}_{\text{cmd}}}=[\omega_{x},\omega_{y},\omega_{z}]^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i}\in[-18,18]\text{rad/s},i\in\{x,y,z\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>rad/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i}\in[-18,18]\text{rad/s},i\in\{x,y,z\}</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined with respect to the quadrotor’s body frame.
Here, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> sec, and the control frequency is 50 Hz for all controllers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Safe set.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The safe set for the quadrotor is defined as <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:p_{z}\leq z_{\text{ceil}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext>ceil</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}=\{x:p_{z}\leq z_{\text{ceil}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\text{ceil}}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext>ceil</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\text{ceil}}=3</annotation></semantics></math>m represents a hard ceiling.
There is no safety constraint for the ground.
Note that <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{S}}(x)=z_{\mathrm{ceil}}-z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ceil</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{S}}(x)=z_{\mathrm{ceil}}-z</annotation></semantics></math> has relative degree 2 for thrust, but the relative degree for bodyrate inputs is higher.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reference trajectory, reward, episode setup.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The quadrotor task tracks a powerloop reference inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, shown in Fig. <a href="#A6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Reference trajectory, reward, episode setup. ‣ F.2 Quadrotor Environment Details ‣ Appendix F Experiment Details ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
The reference follows a vertical circular loop of radius 1.5m centered at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,0,2]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,0,2]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>m, starting at the bottom of the loop with tangential speed 4.5m/s.
The resulting reference completes one full loop in approximately 2.1 sec and is sampled at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> sec.
It is intentionally unsafe, as the loop apex exceeds the ceiling <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\mathrm{ceil}}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ceil</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\mathrm{ceil}}=3</annotation></semantics></math>m, and the tangential speed exceeds the free-fall threshold <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\sqrt{1.5g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\sqrt{1.5g}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=1.1</annotation></semantics></math>) required for dynamic feasibility at the apex <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>.
The attitude reference simultaneously commands an aggressive <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> flip, forcing the controller to trade off near-ceiling translational tracking, agile attitude-rate tracking, and hard safety enforcement at the most dynamically constrained portion of the maneuver.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At step <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the reward is the negative weighted tracking cost</p>
<table id="A6.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{k}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{k}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\Big(w_{p,\mathrm{xy}}\|\mathbf{p}_{x,y}-\mathbf{p}_{{\mathrm{ref}},x,y}\|_{2}^{2}+w_{p,z}(p_{z}-p_{{\mathrm{ref}},z})^{2}+w_{v}\|\mathbf{v}-\mathbf{v}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>xy</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\Big(w_{p,\mathrm{xy}}\|\mathbf{p}_{x,y}-\mathbf{p}_{{\mathrm{ref}},x,y}\|_{2}^{2}+w_{p,z}(p_{z}-p_{{\mathrm{ref}},z})^{2}+w_{v}\|\mathbf{v}-\mathbf{v}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+w_{\mathrm{att}}\|\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{att}}\|_{2}^{2}+\|\mathbf{\omega}_{\mathrm{cmd}}-\mathbf{\omega}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}\|_{W_{\mathbf{\omega}}}^{2}+w_{a}a_{\mathrm{cmd}}^{2}+w_{\Omega}\|\mathbf{\omega}_{\mathrm{cmd}}\|_{2}^{2}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>att</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>att</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>cmd</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+w_{\mathrm{att}}\|\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{att}}\|_{2}^{2}+\|\mathbf{\omega}_{\mathrm{cmd}}-\mathbf{\omega}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}\|_{W_{\mathbf{\omega}}}^{2}+w_{a}a_{\mathrm{cmd}}^{2}+w_{\Omega}\|\mathbf{\omega}_{\mathrm{cmd}}\|_{2}^{2}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{att}}=\operatorname{sgn}(q_{e,w})\,\mathbf{q}_{e,\mathrm{xyz}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>att</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>xyz</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{att}}=\operatorname{sgn}(q_{e,w})\,\mathbf{q}_{e,\mathrm{xyz}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{e}=\mathbf{q}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}\otimes\mathbf{q}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{e}=\mathbf{q}_{{\mathrm{ref}}}\otimes\mathbf{q}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The weights are</p>
<table id="A6.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{p,\mathrm{xy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>xy</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{p,\mathrm{xy}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2.5," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2.5,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{p,z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{p,z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2.0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2.0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4.0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4.0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{\mathrm{att}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>att</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{\mathrm{att}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=16.0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>16.0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=16.0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{\mathbf{\omega}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{\mathbf{\omega}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathrm{diag}}(0.10,0.20,0.05)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathrm{diag}}(0.10,0.20,0.05),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.01," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.01,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.01." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.01.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">As in the unicycle experiment, these weights were selected by fine-tuning a vanilla tracking policy with no safety mechanism, and purely for nominal powerloop tracking of the aggressive position and attitude references shown in Fig. <a href="#A6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Reference trajectory, reward, episode setup. ‣ F.2 Quadrotor Environment Details ‣ Appendix F Experiment Details ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
The environment uses <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> sec and an episode horizon of 106 steps, identical to the length of the powerloop reference.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14536v1/figures/quadrotor_reference_render.png" id="A6.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/208;" width="238" height="208" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Quadrotor powerloop reference trajectory. Note that the powerloop includes an aggressive attitude reference that commands a full <math id="A6.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> flip at the apex.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>PS2-RL Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.1 </span>Unicycle: Phase I</h4>

<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Base set and controller.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}=[0,\ v_{{\mathrm{des}}},\ 0]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>des</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}=[0,\ v_{{\mathrm{des}}},\ 0]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be the cruising equilibrium, with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{{\mathrm{des}}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>des</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{{\mathrm{des}}}=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\star}=\mathbf{0}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\star}=\mathbf{0}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the local error state <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(x)=[\,y,\;v-v_{{\mathrm{des}}},\;\psi\,]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>des</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(x)=[\,y,\;v-v_{{\mathrm{des}}},\;\psi\,]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We linearize (<a href="#A6.E125" title="In System dynamics. ‣ F.1 Unicycle Environment Details ‣ Appendix F Experiment Details ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">125</span></a>) about <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{\star},u^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{\star},u^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> and discretize it with the same <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> sec as the environment timestep.
We then solve the discrete-time LQR problem for <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{d},B_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{d},B_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the discretized linearization, with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d}={\mathrm{diag}}(1,1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d}={\mathrm{diag}}(1,1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{d}={\mathrm{diag}}(0.01,0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{d}={\mathrm{diag}}(0.01,0.5)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> be the positive-definite solution of the discrete algebraic Riccati equation and</p>
<table id="A6.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K=(R_{d}+B_{d}^{\top}PB_{d})^{-1}B_{d}^{\top}PA_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K=(R_{d}+B_{d}^{\top}PB_{d})^{-1}B_{d}^{\top}PA_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, the base controller is the LQR feedback</p>
<table id="A6.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\mathcal{B}}(x)=-Ke(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\mathcal{B}}(x)=-Ke(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(128)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where we clip the resulting control input to be within <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The base set is the ellipsoid</p>
<table id="A6.EGx126" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{B}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:e(x)^{\top}Pe(x)\leq c_{\mathcal{B}}\},\qquad h_{\mathcal{B}}(x)=c_{\mathcal{B}}-e(x)^{\top}Pe(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{B}}=\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:e(x)^{\top}Pe(x)\leq c_{\mathcal{B}}\},\qquad h_{\mathcal{B}}(x)=c_{\mathcal{B}}-e(x)^{\top}Pe(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathcal{B}}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathcal{B}}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.
The actuator-admissible upper bound for the LQR ellipsoid is</p>
<table id="A6.EGx127" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{c}=\min\left\{\frac{a_{\max}^{2}}{K_{a}P^{-1}K_{a}^{\top}},\frac{r_{\max}^{2}}{K_{r}P^{-1}K_{r}^{\top}}\right\}\approx 1.05," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.05</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{c}=\min\left\{\frac{a_{\max}^{2}}{K_{a}P^{-1}K_{a}^{\top}},\frac{r_{\max}^{2}}{K_{r}P^{-1}K_{r}^{\top}}\right\}\approx 1.05,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are the acceleration and yaw-rate rows of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Hence <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathcal{B}}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathcal{B}}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> keeps the unclipped LQR action strictly within the input limits over <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding coordinate radii are approximately <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y|\leq 0.209" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.209</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y|\leq 0.209</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|v-v_{{\mathrm{des}}}|\leq 0.342" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>des</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.342</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|v-v_{{\mathrm{des}}}|\leq 0.342</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\psi|\leq 0.110" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.110</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\psi|\leq 0.110</annotation></semantics></math>, well inside the safe bounds <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y|\leq 1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y|\leq 1.8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\psi|\leq\pi/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\psi|\leq\pi/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Design region and reference measure.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We instantiate the design region as the following box</p>
<table id="A6.EGx128" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega=\left\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:|y|\leq 1.8,\,v\in[0,\,12],\,|\psi|\leq\frac{\pi}{3}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>1.8</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 12</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega=\left\{x\in{\mathcal{X}}:|y|\leq 1.8,\,v\in[0,\,12],\,|\psi|\leq\frac{\pi}{3}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subseteq{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> covers the entire safety-relevant portion of the state space.
The reference measure underlying <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{SA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>SA</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{SA}}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken to be the uniform measure on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we approximate at evaluation time by a uniform <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="201\times 121\times 201" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>201</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>121</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>201</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">201\times 121\times 201</annotation></semantics></math> grid over <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,v,\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,v,\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We count the grid points that safely arrive at <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> within horizon <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> sec under <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and divide by the total number of grid points in <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Safe-arrival policy backbone.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Phase I instantiates Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ E.6 Phase I: Safe-Arrival Policy Training ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with a TD3-style off-policy backbone <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>.
We maintain a deterministic actor <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\mathrm{SA}}^{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and twin safe-arrival critics <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{1}_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{1}_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{2}_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>SA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{2}_{\mathrm{SA},\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, each with their corresponding target networks updated via Polyak averaging.
Both critics are trained with the discounted safe-arrival Bellman recursion (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2 Safe-Arrival Value Function ‣ 4 Provably Safe, yet Scalable RL ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) using a Huber loss.
Episodes terminate on first-hit entry into the base set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> (success) or the failure set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> (failure).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Curriculum and initial-state sampling.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initial states are drawn from a curriculum-controlled distribution <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>arr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{arr}}</annotation></semantics></math> that progressively expands during training.
Concretely, we maintain a scalar curriculum scale <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, initialized at <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, and sample initial states uniformly from</p>
<table id="A6.EGx129" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y\sim\mathcal{U}(-y_{s},y_{s}),\quad v\sim v_{{\mathrm{des}}}+\mathcal{U}(-v_{s},v_{s}),\quad\psi\sim\mathcal{U}(-\psi_{s},\psi_{s})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>des</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y\sim\mathcal{U}(-y_{s},y_{s}),\quad v\sim v_{{\mathrm{des}}}+\mathcal{U}(-v_{s},v_{s}),\quad\psi\sim\mathcal{U}(-\psi_{s},\psi_{s}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each radius <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{s},v_{s}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{s},v_{s},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> interpolates linearly with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
We reject any sample that lies inside the base set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that all training initial states belong to <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The scale <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is incremented by <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.005</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.005</annotation></semantics></math> whenever the rolling success rate over a window of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> episodes exceeds <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, with at least <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> episodes between increments.
This mild curriculum starts the policy from states close to <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where short safe arrivals are easy to discover, and progressively pushes the initial-state distribution outward to cover most of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> once the policy has learned to recover from such states.
Note that curriculum learning is an optimization heuristic we employ, not a required component of safe-arrival policy training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The full hyperparameters are summarized in Table <a href="#A6.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Control-invariant layer parameters. ‣ F.3.2 Unicycle: Phase II ‣ F.3 PS2-RL Implementation Details ‣ Appendix F Experiment Details ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.2 </span>Unicycle: Phase II</h4>

<section id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PS2 policy backbone.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Phase II is instantiated with a SAC backbone <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> for the policy <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the control-invariant layer <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{CIL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>CIL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{CIL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is appended to its output.
The composed backup policy <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> from Phase I is fixed, and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{CIL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>CIL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{CIL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed from the BCBF rollout of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi_{b}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi_{b}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> as described in App. <a href="#A5.SS7" title="E.7 Phase II: Control-Invariant Layer and PS2 Policy ‣ Appendix E PS2-RL Details and Proofs ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.7</span></a>.
During both data collection and policy updates, the nominal SAC action is projected through the control-invariant layer before being applied to the environment.
Thus, the replay buffer stores projected controls, the actor loss evaluates the critic at projected actions, and target actions in Bellman updates are also projected.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The SAC actor is a tanh-squashed Gaussian policy, and evaluation uses the deterministic mean action followed by the same projection.
Initial states are sampled uniformly from <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}_{T}}({\pi_{b}^{\star}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Episodes have a fixed horizon of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> steps, matching the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>-second sinusoidal reference with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Control-invariant layer parameters.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unicycle safety set has four scalar inequalities, and the terminal base condition is the single LQR ellipsoid <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{B}}(x)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{B}}(x)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
With <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> second and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta t}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta t}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=20</annotation></semantics></math> backup steps.
Thus, the finite-mesh BCBF construction contributes <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4(N+1)+1=85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4(N+1)+1=85</annotation></semantics></math> BCBF rows.
Together with the input box and the numerical slack nonnegativity row, the implemented QP has <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>90</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90</annotation></semantics></math> inequalities.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The full hyperparameters are summarized in Table <a href="#A6.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Control-invariant layer parameters. ‣ F.3.2 Unicycle: Phase II ‣ F.3 PS2-RL Implementation Details ‣ Appendix F Experiment Details ‣ Provably Safe, Yet ScalableReinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
